From: Alan Shearer
Subject: virtio_net: free interrupts if queue interrupt setup fails

Applies after virtio-net-mutex-uninit (err7).

setup_interrupt() can succeed and a later queue_setup_interrupt() can
fail. init_device then returns an error; uninit_device is not called, so
the device interrupt stays configured.

uninit_device already calls free_interrupts() before mutex_destroy().
Do the same on the init failure path. setup_interrupt() failure still
goes to err7: there is nothing to free. Queue-interrupt failures after
it succeeds go to err8.

Does not free_queues() on earlier labels. That is a separate leftover.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
@@ -441,8 +441,8 @@
 	status = info->virtio->queue_setup_interrupt(info->rxQueues[0],
 		virtio_net_rxDone, info);
 	if (status != B_OK) {
 		ERROR("queue interrupt setup failed (%s)\n", strerror(status));
-		goto err7;
+		goto err8;
 	}
 
 	status = info->virtio->queue_setup_interrupt(info->txQueues[0],
@@ -449,7 +449,7 @@
 		virtio_net_txDone, info);
 	if (status != B_OK) {
 		ERROR("queue interrupt setup failed (%s)\n", strerror(status));
-		goto err7;
+		goto err8;
 	}
 
 	if ((info->features & VIRTIO_NET_F_CTRL_VQ) != 0) {
@@ -458,12 +458,14 @@
 			NULL, info);
 		if (status != B_OK) {
 			ERROR("queue interrupt setup failed (%s)\n", strerror(status));
-			goto err7;
+			goto err8;
 		}
 	}
 
 	*_cookie = info;
 	return B_OK;
 
+err8:
+	info->virtio->free_interrupts(info->virtio_device);
 err7:
 	mutex_destroy(&info->rxLock);
 	mutex_destroy(&info->txLock);
